# Codex CLI project config for consumer projects (merged into
# .codex/config.toml by `mcpctl init project-mcp`). The server runs via
# `mcpctl run` and defaults its project root to the cwd. The hooks below are
# scripts in .agents/ that resolve their own project root.

[mcp_servers.project-mcp]
command = "/usr/local/bin/mcpctl"
args = ["run", "project-mcp"]

# Counterparts to the .claude/settings.json hooks. One entry per matcher
# (`mcpctl init` merges hook entries by matcher, so a matcher listed twice
# would be folded together and run its hooks twice).

# Blocks cold source exploration (grep/rg/find/cat) until project-mcp has been
# consulted once this session.
[[hooks.PreToolUse]]
matcher = "Bash"

  [[hooks.PreToolUse.hooks]]
  type = "command"
  command = ".agents/hooks/project-mcp-session-gate.sh"

# Reminds the agent to consult project-mcp before each TDD decision point.
[[hooks.PreToolUse]]
matcher = "mcp__outside-in-tdd__init_feature|mcp__outside-in-tdd__drill_down|mcp__outside-in-tdd__write_test|mcp__outside-in-tdd__write_test_skeleton|mcp__outside-in-tdd__write_code"

  [[hooks.PreToolUse.hooks]]
  type = "command"
  command = ".agents/hooks/project-mcp-reminder.sh"

# Records that project-mcp was consulted, which unlocks the gate and resets the
# reminder.
[[hooks.PostToolUse]]
matcher = "mcp__project-mcp__find_symbol|mcp__project-mcp__get_symbol_context|mcp__project-mcp__get_dependencies|mcp__project-mcp__get_dependents|mcp__project-mcp__get_project_overview"

  [[hooks.PostToolUse.hooks]]
  type = "command"
  command = ".agents/hooks/project-mcp-mark-consulted.sh"
